{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"215278c5-9eb9-45bd-91d9-cfb752b4b601","status":"SUCCESS","response":"## 1. Functionality Understanding Statement (`/functionality-understanding-check`)\n\nIn strict alignment with [`LANGUAGE.md`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/LANGUAGE.md) and [`functional_specification_008.md`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/functional_specification_008.md), the desired `{functionality}` is to cleanly separate and synchronize **Regional Medicare DME MAC Jurisdictions** (`JURIS-DME-A`, `JURIS-DME-B`, `JURIS-DME-C`, `JURIS-DME-D`) and **Individual Geographic States** (all 50 US states plus DC and territories) across the UI navigation controls, backend topology filtering API, and GraphRAG retrieval pipeline:\n\n1. **Dual Cascading Navigation Controls ([`FilterToolbar.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/frontend/src/components/FilterToolbar.tsx), [`GraphSyncContext.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/frontend/src/context/GraphSyncContext.tsx), [`App.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/frontend/src/App.tsx)):**\n   - Replace the single conflated dropdown with two distinct selectors labeled `JURISDICTION:` and `STATE:`.\n   - `JURISDICTION:` lists `All Jurisdictions (National Overview)` and all 4 regional DME MAC zones (`Jurisdiction A (Northeast - Noridian)`, `Jurisdiction B (Midwest - CGS)`, `Jurisdiction C (South - CGS)`, `Jurisdiction D (West - Noridian)`). Selecting a jurisdiction highlights `JURIS-DME-*` and its `COVERS_STATE` states on the canvas and cascades the `STATE:` selector to show only states assigned to that jurisdiction.\n   - `STATE:` lists `All States (Overview)` and all 50 US states (plus DC, PR, VI) in alphabetical order. Selecting a state loads that state's localized non-rural `FeeScheduleEntry` nodes and automatically updates `JURISDICTION:` to reflect its legally assigned regional contractor.\n2. **Multi-Tier Topology Filtering ([`src/api/routes.py`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/api/routes.py)):**\n   - `GET /api/graph/topology` accepts both `jurisdiction_filter` and `state_filter` independently:\n     - **National Overview (`All`):** Returns all 4 jurisdictions and all 53 states with fee schedules collapsed (`155` nodes, maintaining 60 FPS).\n     - **Jurisdiction-Level Filter:** Returns root policy, governing change requests, coverage policies, the selected `JURIS-DME-*` contractor node, and only the states covered via `COVERS_STATE`, with fee schedules collapsed by default.\n     - **State-Level Filter:** Returns the selected state, its parent regional contractor, governing change requests/coverage policies, and all 71 localized non-rural `FeeScheduleEntry` nodes for that state (`171` nodes).\n     - Fails fast with HTTP 400 (`EntityResolutionError`) on unrecognized state or jurisdiction codes.\n3. **GraphRAG Regional \u0026 Cross-Jurisdiction Integration ([`entity_linker.py`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/graphrag/entity_linker.py), [`traversal.py`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/graphrag/traversal.py), [`context_assembler.py`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/graphrag/context_assembler.py), [`pipeline.py`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/graphrag/pipeline.py), [`models.py`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/graphrag/models.py)):**\n   - Natively resolves and traverses regional contractor inquiries without requiring a state or diagnosis code (e.g., *\"What states does Jurisdiction B cover?\"*, *\"What policies does CGS administer?\"*) and single-state administrative inquiries (e.g., *\"Who administers Medicare Part B DME claims in Texas?\"*, *\"What contractor covers Florida?\"*).\n   - Extracts multiple state anchors and executes comparative state+HCPCS traversals and context assembly across regional boundaries (e.g., *\"Compare allowable rates for A6522 between California and New York.\"*).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Wayfinder Roadmap \u0026 Resolved Decision Tickets\n\n- **Wayfinder Map:** [`wayfinder/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/map.md`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/wayfinder/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/map.md)\n- **Resolved Tickets:**\n  1. [`Ticket 001: Multi-Tier Graph Topology Filtering Contract (/api/graph/topology)`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/wayfinder/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/tickets/ticket-001.md)\n  2. [`Ticket 002: Authoritative 50-State \u0026 4-Jurisdiction Frontend Registry and Bidirectional Cascading Sync Bus`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/wayfinder/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/tickets/ticket-002.md)\n  3. [`Ticket 003: Dual Jurisdiction and State Navigation Selectors (FilterToolbar.tsx)`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/wayfinder/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/tickets/ticket-003.md)\n  4. [`Ticket 004: Multi-State and Regional Contractor Entity Anchor Resolution (EntityAnchorLinker)`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/wayfinder/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/tickets/ticket-004.md)\n  5. [`Ticket 005: Regional Jurisdiction Lineage and Cross-Jurisdiction Comparative GraphRAG Traversal \u0026 Context Assembly`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/wayfinder/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/tickets/ticket-005.md)\n- **Master Component-to-Edit Matrix:** [`wayfinder/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/master_edit_matrix.md`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/wayfinder/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/master_edit_matrix.md)\n- **Handoff Manifest:** [`handoff/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/wayfinder-read-and-plan.txt`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/handoff/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/wayfinder-read-and-plan.txt)\n\n---\n\n## 3. Documentation Sufficiency Certification (`/documentation-sufficient?`)\n\nEvaluated against [`LANGUAGE.md`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/LANGUAGE.md), the planning documentation is certified **`{sufficient}`**:\n- Every targeted file path, line range, class/function signature, Cypher query structure, state contract, and fail-fast validation rule is locked with zero ambiguity.\n- All live Neo4j node and relationship schemas (`Jurisdiction`, `State`, `FeeScheduleEntry`, `COVERS_STATE`, `APPLIES_TO_JURISDICTION`, `HAS_FEE_SCHEDULE`, `APPLIES_TO`) have been empirically verified against the active database.\n\n\u003cpromise\u003eCOMPLETE\u003c/promise\u003e\n","duration_seconds":728.698587,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":244274,"output_tokens":63062,"thinking_tokens":31235,"cache_read_tokens":3506785,"total_tokens":307336}}}
